.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1200 AM PDT Sat Aug 1 2026
(Sunday through Friday)

Subtle cooling each day from Sunday through Wednesday thanks to a
flattening upper level ridge with a passing trough to the north.
Widespread Moderate HeatRisk across the interior will decrease in
coverage through Wednesday. Still expect breezy conditions each
afternoon/evening with onshore flow. The exception will be a
strong offshore flow burst Sunday night into Monday. Not strong
enough for a Wind Adv, but definitely elevate Fire Weather
concerns.

Longer range guidance and official forecast shows a rebound in
temperatures Thursday and Friday as the ridge re-builds over the
region.

